- The numbers are calculated live from your tasks/{taskId} in Firebase Realtime Database.

## Manage My Tasks - CRUD

- You will have 4 basic things you can do with any task in your portal.
- It’s like a to-do list for your course, but saved in Firebase. 

The CRUD

### C = Create - Add a new task

- You click "Add Task" and fill in:
1. Title: "E.g Complete Array Exercise
2. Due Date: 15 Aug
3. Priority: High, category: JavaScript

### R = Read - View/see your tasks.

- The Dashboard and Task List pull all your tasks where[userId/user name] from Firebase and display them.
- You can also search, filter, or sort using JavaScript array methods:
1. filter() = show only "outstanding/completed" tasks.
2. sort () = sort by (dueDate/Date). "Show me all my high priority tasks due this week.

### U = Update - Change/edit a task

- You can click on a task and edit the title, due date, priority, or category.
- Dashboard numbers like Progress % recalculate automatically.

### D = Delete - Remove a task

- The task you are deleting will be removed from taskId in Firebase.
- The Dashboard numbers like Progress % recalculate automatically after deletion.

## Book Support

- You are stuck on a function. You can go to "Book Support" and fill out the form: topic, notes. 
- When you submit, it saves to bookings/{bookingId} with status: Pending.
- When your assessor sees it, it will update to "Confirmed". Then you will get your status feedback.

